    },
    {
      "text": "Pangea Design",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Variable Angle Locking Technology**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Pangea’s variable angle locking technology uses a CoCr locking screw, which is harder than the Ti6Al4V ELI plate, allowing for the screwhead’s threads to form a definitive locking position in the plate’s locking hole by engaging the softer, Ti6Al4V ELI material.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423211/images/e924125a-a88c-49c8-921d-9c080b53e5a1_screenshot_2025-01-14_at_3.25.53_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "This technology allows the user to aim and lock the screw into the plate within a true 30° cone of the predetermined hole trajectory. The variable angle drill guide provided with the system offers guidance with respect to the limit of the 30° cone. The locking mechanism remains functional for up to three attempts at locking screw insertion.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Circular holes that accommodate screws are universal, accepting non-locking screws and locking screws within a 30° cone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Hybrid LC Holes (locking/compression)**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Hybrid LC Holes allow for either active compression with the use of a non-locking screw in the compression section of the hole or variable angle locking with the use of a locking screw in the universal section of the hole. If locking is not desired, the universal section of the hole also accepts non-locking screws. Each Hybrid LC Hole is designed to provide up to 2mm of compression.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**2.0mm Proximal Suture Holes with Undercuts**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Allows for suture threading after plate placement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Proximal Cluster of Screws**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Designed for screw fixation of the proximal tibia, while addressing metadiaphyseal fractures that may need compression",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423211/images/9be6f1d5-b5a0-472d-aab0-3173afa6b2cc_screenshot_2025-01-14_at_3.26.13_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Kickstand Screw**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Designed to provide support for the medial tibia plateau",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Waisted Scalloped Shape**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Robust Plate**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Thicker than the other Pangea Proximal Tibia Plates and utilizes the large fragment screw platform for plating of proximal tibia fractures involving the metaphysis and meta diaphysis.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423211/images/9be6f1d5-b5a0-472d-aab0-3173afa6b2cc_screenshot_2025-01-14_at_3.26.13_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**2.0mm Distal K-Wire Hole**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "To provide temporary fixation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Placement",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "This plate is placed on the anterolateral surface of the proximal tibia.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Designed for single implant fixation of proximal tibial fractures and non-unions where increased construct rigidity is necessary",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Proper position is achieved when the proximal end of the plate is adjacent to the articular surface, allowing for the proximal screws to support the joint surface.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fit",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pangea Extra Articular Proximal Tibia Plate is designed to aid in the treatment of bicondylar fractures, allowing for treatment with a lateral plate and one incision.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "This plate is designed for single implant fixation of proximal tibial fractures and non-unions where increased plate rigidity is necessary.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Designed with the use of SOMA: Stryker Orthopedics Modeling and Analytics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "SOMA analysis shows the Extra Articular Proximal Tibia plate fits closer to the bone compared to Synthes LCP Proximal Tibia plates. 2",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Indications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Pangea Tibia Plating System is indicated for the internal fixation and stabilization of tibia bone fractures and osteotomies in normal and osteopenic bone, including:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Diaphyseal, metaphyseal, epiphyseal, extra- and intra-articular fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Non-unions, malunions, and deformities",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Periprosthetic fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
